<h2>B. Quantitative Analysis</h2>
<p>Comparing Algorithm 1 (Base CNN) and Algorithm 2 (Base CNN-LSTM) confirms the observations of Barona L&oacute;pez et al. [1]: adding recurrent cells improves post-processed sequence accuracy from 62.40% to 70.67% (+8.27 percentage points) and Macro F1 from 55.54% to 68.76% (+13.22 percentage points). In our trial-level setting, temporal recurrence captures continuous contraction dynamics that frame-independent CNNs miss.</p>

<p>Algorithm 3 (Enhanced CNN with Focal Loss) achieved only 42.80% accuracy, demonstrating that without recurrent temporal context, frame-independent focal loss leads to severe gradient instability during transient gesture onsets.</p>

<p>Algorithm 4 (Proposed AttnInceptionHGR) reached the highest overall sequence accuracy (72.00%) and highest Macro F1-score (72.60%), improving over the reference base paper by +1.33% in accuracy (10 additional correct sequences out of 750) and +3.84 percentage points in Macro F1.</p>

